# Artifactory Conda Config Resource

Manages the instance-wide **Enable Conda shards** checkbox under **Administration > Artifactory Settings > Packages Settings > Conda**. Define only one resource per Artifactory instance. This setting applies to local, remote and virtual Conda repositories.

The Artifactory deployment must expose the Conda sharding setting through its Packages Settings API. The resource uses the UI's `artifactory/ui/generalConfig` endpoint and preserves unrelated settings when saving. Coordinate changes with other administrators: the endpoint does not expose an ETag for conditional writes, so concurrent global configuration edits can be overwritten.

Enabling sharding does not reindex existing local repositories. Reindex those repositories after enablement and use a client that supports sharded repodata. Legacy `repodata.json` and `current_repodata.json` endpoints remain available. See [JFrog's Conda metadata sharding instructions](https://docs.jfrog.com/artifactory/docs/conda-repositories#enable-conda-metadata-sharding).

Removing this resource leaves Artifactory's Conda settings unchanged. To disable sharding, apply `shards_enabled = false` before removing the resource.

